      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "No NOFA published as of November 8, 2026. Staff report (August 11, 2026) says the County will score proposals for Rounds 4 and 5 jointly with the two cities once the MOU extension is executed by both city councils.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "unclear",
      "layering_notes": "Nevada County's Housing and Community Services Department (HCS, Tyler Barrington, Director, 950 Maidu Ave, Nevada City, 530-265-1645, Housing@nevadacountyca.gov) sits inside the Health and Human Services Agency and administers the Western Nevada County Regional Housing Trust Fund, PLHA (as delegated applicant for Grass Valley and Nevada City), state HOME and CDBG awards, the MORE mobile home program and the new Down Payment Assistance Program; the Behavioral Health and Homelessness Department (Cari Yardley, Director) holds Homekey+, BHSA and the Truckee Navigation Center; HHAP is administered by the Homeless Resource Council of the Sierras as the CoC CA-531 lead; and the Regional Housing Authority (Sutter, Nevada, Yuba, Colusa and Lake counties, Yuba City) supplies vouchers. Grass Valley, Nevada City and Truckee run their own programs (Pass 3). The County has no inclusionary ordinance, no housing impact fee and no affordable housing fee waiver program; the only land use incentive is the state density bonus ordinance. nevadacountyca.gov opens directly and the Legistar web API client 'nevco' exposes staff reports and attachments at legistar.granicus.com/nevco/attachments/. PLHA is small (roughly $200,000 to $300,000 a year countywide) and has historically been bundled into trust fund loans. A developer with a site in the unincorporated area, Grass Valley or Nevada City should contact HCS early to be placed in the Round 4 and 5 pipeline; awards will be 55-year deferred loans suitable as TCAC local contribution. Round 3 money is committed to Lone Oak II and Habitat.",
      "source_url": "https://nevco.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=49657&GUID=75673352-4F30-44D4-8EC5-795532A21A21",
      "record_id": "dbfc894af3",
      "cycle_notes": "",
      "eligible_project_detail": [
        "new construction multifamily rental",
        "acquisition/rehab",
        "owner-occupied affordable housing",
        "homeless services and interim housing"
      ],
      "next_deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_check": "no_date",
      "link_status": "ok",
      "prevailing_wage_basis": "No stated rule: the 2024-2028 PLHA Formula Guidelines (https://www.hcd.ca.gov/sites/default/files/docs/grants-and-funding/plha/2024-2028-plha-formula-guidelines.pdf) contain no prevailing wage provision, and the County's PLHA amendment staff report and Resolution 26-317 certifications (https://legistar.granicus.com/nevco/attachments/7d500d37-79a8-450c-820d-b92b30542adf.pdf) are silent. Coverage of a County PLHA loan is a general Labor Code 1720(b) question that turns on 1720(c) exemptions, including the 1720(c)(6)(E) affordable housing exemption applied in DIR PW 2006-020, and on any HOME or CDBG layered in the trust fund loan.",
